# The shelf holds what the agents produce, and most of it is versioned. Handoffs
# are the exception: CSTs are transient by design (deleted on ingest; nothing
# auto-deletes — `handoff-store list` age-flags strays), they are chmod 600, and
# they carry raw conversation context. Tracking a
# file built to delete itself is churn; tracking one built to hold session
# contents is worse.
home/.claude/shelf/handoffs/
home/.claude/shelf/boot-digest.stamp

# yt-transcripts are the shelf's second exception, for the same reason as handoffs:
# they are bulky downloads (a 50-min talk is ~550 KB of raw .vtt), they re-download
# from youtube in seconds, and the skill's `transit` mode deletes them on purpose.
# Tracking a store one of whose modes is "delete immediately" is pure churn.
home/.claude/shelf/yt-transcripts/

# The sounds shelf holds game audio Dima ripped by hand — assets we have no
# right to redistribute, and binaries git has no business storing. audition.sh
# is the only thing here we wrote; approved.txt and candidates/ are his picking
# state, rebuilt by running the TUI again.
home/.claude/shelf/sounds/*
!home/.claude/shelf/sounds/audition.sh

# The cclio-mode snapshot is a build (script/skill-cclio-mode-snapshot.ts), recompiled at every halt.
home/.claude/shelf/cclio-mode-snapshot.md

# The memory-sync mirror is a build too (script/skill-memory-sync-mirror.ts): the cc masters rendered
# into cw memory entries plus a manifest, re-rendered by x-cw:memory-sync and at every halt.
home/.claude/shelf/memory-sync-mirror/
__pycache__/
home/.claude/shelf/ci-seen.json
home/.claude/shelf/jev/route.log

# Runtime state written by scheduled jobs, not source. The cowork gazette heartbeat
# is written on anthropic's machines and lands here; nothing in the repo produces it.
schedule/state/

# Seed for hotkeys/map.html, rewritten by `pnpm hotkeys:scan`. A snapshot of this mac's
# app preferences, not source — and biome reformats it while the generator re-emits raw json,
# so committing it means a tree that is dirty after every scan. The page names the command
# when it is absent.
hotkeys/hotkeys.js
hotkeys/presses.js

# gmailctl's oauth client and token live beside the config it reads; secrets, never source.
gmail/credentials.json
gmail/token.json
